      "disposition": "Further investigation",
      "failing": true,
      "risk_accepted": false,
      "release_blocking": true,
      "technical_justification": "The exact Minecraft chat path sends server-controlled text to the [CHAT] Log4j logger in 1.14.4 and 1.17.1. On all three exact Linux runtime samples, Mojang launcher XML kept the marker literal and the local synthetic context received zero calls. Under embedded fallback XML, Log4j 2.14.1 issued two local synthetic JNDI calls; Log4j 2.8.1 issued none with manifest Patchy-first order but issued two when the test reversed the classpath. The JDK LDAP decoder accepted a harmless serialized String on Linux JRE 8u202 and Java 16.0.1, while Java 17.0.15 blocked it. No network lookup or gadget was used. Thus the default metadata configuration mitigates the tested chat path, but the underlying JNDI path is reachable under alternate logging/classpath conditions and the Java 8/16 runtimes accept LDAP serialized data.",
